From 7edee22736d6f1e9d48dd941bef909ebb3cb676e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:02:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 57/58] soundwire: support TCL firmware nodes and controller
 rebinding

The supplemental SoundWire masters describe port configuration and codec
children through firmware properties. The controller and core need to
consume that representation and clean up partial child enumeration;
rebind must also account for inherited runtime-PM state.

Add firmware-node slave discovery with reference cleanup, property
readers with range/count checks for controller ports, and the TCL master
platform IDs. Reset runtime-PM bookkeeping on the relevant probe/remove
path and use the existing reset/re-enumeration mechanism when an empty
bus cannot enter clock stop. These changes require repeated bind/PCM/PM
validation. They do not change the slave-status indexing loop or
establish the cause of the observed TX Alert.
